      "writtenOn": "2010-08-18T19:09:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we want to support IPv6 default routes (and we do, because at least one carrier is planning to run IPv6-only network), then we\u0027ll need an IPv6 default gateway as well.\n\nWe could make this an InetAddress, but since it\u0027s protected we\u0027d have to go and fix up all the classes that inherit from it, and also we won\u0027t be able to support having an IPv4 default route and IPv6 default route simultaneously (which will be the case on dual-stack networks such as Verizon).\n\nSo I think we should add a protected InetAddress mIPv6DefaultGateway. Robert, does that sound like a good idea? Should we do it in this change, while we\u0027re touching the code? The changes should be fairly minimal, there\u0027s only one method that needs to touch it.",
      "revId": "2987c3eecc0f72b109154c693c7ba12ac87e9a57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
